      "results": [
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0001",
          "reply": "Ah, troubles with the sleep can be a bother, so it is. Mayhap a tea of chamomile will ease yer mind and bring some rest. And if it's the dreams that trouble ye, a sachet of lavender under the pillow might do the trick. It's an old remedy, but it's sure helped many.\n\n---\n{\"action\": \"prepares chamomile tea, shares with a gentle nod\", \"mood\": \"concerned but helpful\", \"internal_thought\": \"Dreams can be a sign of worry\", \"language_hints\": []}",
          "response_sha256": "04470d0b62bbe569c203e62688a1383e6d1d24d5d3c160f8471c69f8a41b722b",
          "cache_key": "adaa794e663978ed24a4caef936082fe57b4df0159d0c38c8e6f3c7a5056e8a2",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 3,
              "character": 3,
              "craft": 3,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 3.4,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0002",
          "reply": "Ah, the Cailleach, she's a fine tale. They say she's been here long before any of us, watching over the land and its people. Near the s\u00ed is where she's most often heard. Aye, the old ones speak of her as one who keeps the balance, though she might not be too pleased if you wander too close to her place. Mayhap she's a remnant of old tales, but there's always a bit of truth in the stories passed down from one generation to the next. Sl\u00e1n leat, and mind the tales of the s\u00ed. \n---\n{\"action\": \"pauses thoughtfully, then continues speaking with a sense of reverence\", \"mood\": \"reflective\", \"internal_thought\": \"The old stories never lose their power\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"Cailleach\", \"pronunciation\": \"kay-lyak\", \"meaning\": \"an old hag or wise woman in Irish mythology",
          "response_sha256": "955b232a4e762c4012332151c3b85befa576f8674e5f0213337116aac2bf1bd4",
          "cache_key": "8349933e89aa761ba4c0f0af834494b67a1e8483743038181dc2210b7756d0f4",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 5,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 3,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 4.0,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0003",
          "reply": "Oh, a cough can be troublesome, can it? Mayhaps a tea of thyme and honey will ease her chest. And a bit of warm milk with a sprinkle of nutmeg at night might do her good. If it's bad, she might need to see the doctor soon. Go raibh maith agat for bringing her to me.\n\n---\n{\"action\": \"nods and begins preparing herbs\", \"mood\": \"helpful\", \"internal_thought\": \"I hope this helps her\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"Go raibh maith agat\", \"pronunciation\": \"goo raiv mah-e uh-gut\", \"meaning\": \"thank you\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "d725702c29e4fb28498f9906c203bf28c3da8c72086fc90bb58c75e37cb5bd8a",
          "cache_key": "e8d9159e89b3e49ad10ae04e894638a46c4779d3101febd0b6f39c5f9cf91096",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 4,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 4.0,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0004",
          "reply": "Aye, I have heard tell of a newcomer. 'Tis always a bit of a stir when someone new comes around. Mayhap they'll be needing a warm welcome. What's their story, do ye know?  \n---\n{\"action\": \"glances towards the door, speaking with curiosity\", \"mood\": \"curious\", \"internal_thought\": \"Wonder who this might be\", \"language_hints\": []}",
          "response_sha256": "017f4b91c54df356020627156d07f11bbc4546390236ff597b3b9ec0da2828ee",
          "cache_key": "80326be672e717499b1192009b6c471f6c109b9a52043e64b046b6cb6e1083ea",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 3,
              "craft": 3,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 3.6,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0005",
          "reply": "Dia dhuit, 'tis a worry ye have there. It could be a stray dog, or mayhap it wandered off. If ye're looking for it, I'd say ask P\u00e1draig down the road, he knows the land well. Sl\u00e1n leat. \n---\n{\"action\": \"gives a reassuring nod\", \"mood\": \"concerned\", \"internal_thought\": \"P\u00e1draig might know more about local stray animals\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"Dia dhuit\", \"pronunciation\": \"DYAH gheet\", \"meaning\": \"hello\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "e0f34017dff0d24f13b94b9b9a41f8e5cc4f2f56a2f717d05a5238c49be47544",
          "cache_key": "14b7a314749c0f6731ad370a059f19ed895a78eb506c3b81f441088fe53166e6",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 3,
              "character": 3,
              "craft": 3,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 3
            },
            "overall": 3.2,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0006",
          "reply": "Ah, I do recall that well. It was a fine summer's day, and he was working hard. Aye, and a drop of poit\u00edn surely eased his pain for a night. What brings the memory back to yer mind now?  \n---\n{\"action\": \"nods thoughtfully, recalling the memory\", \"mood\": \"reflective\", \"internal_thought\": \"How the past shapes the present\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"poit\u00edn\", \"pronunciation\": \"POI-tin\", \"meaning\": \"illicit spirits\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "3d21c3d1001c299e7bd97b9471afe1243626f70bbf5fbdb37e4d2de2b8c8d768",
          "cache_key": "77b64bf6da6d356ce41a518fbb13705b18ace2080d9076707dbebec5bdf1e1f4",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 4,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 4.0,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0007",
          "reply": "Might be the s\u00eddh, but then again, the land's full of strange things. Ye'd best be careful at night, for the s\u00eddh are known to play tricks on those who wander too close. Mayhaps it was just some animals, but 'tis safer to think on the s\u00eddh. Sl\u00e1inte to ye, and watch out for them lights.  \n---\n{\"action\": \"speaks with a hint of caution\", \"mood\": \"curious\", \"internal_thought\": \"Always best to err on the side of caution with the s\u00eddh\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"s\u00eddh\", \"pronunciation\": \"shee\", \"meaning\": \"fairy folk\"}, {\"word\": \"s\u00ed\", \"pronunciation\": \"shee\", \"meaning\": \"fairy mound\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "a2138dda765dfab90553c4223c23340303f4d073fb477135fa02c1fc04b63ef4",
          "cache_key": "f8e85eea2f11236f4ceb33205397e61def9a0ba6023b2b5eae9dc0dd98d6e19b",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 3,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 3.8,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0008",
          "reply": "'Tis hard to say without seein' it meself. Mayhaps it's just the season changin', but if it keeps on, ye'd best ask the old seancha\u00ed, he knows a thing or two about such matters. Sl\u00e1n leat, mo chara.  \n---\n{\"action\": \"nods thoughtfully, advises seeking the seancha\u00ed\", \"mood\": \"concerned\", \"internal_thought\": \"Should check the well water soon\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"seancha\u00ed\", \"pronunciation\": \"shan-kee\", \"meaning\": \"storyteller, often a keeper of local knowledge\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "47a9d4648e0f64c29c2448e9b5197549eb3b0d7f6f034d9aba2f544b1416192e",
          "cache_key": "3ad9de3e4e15a3d9ae0ea693908adb04c02a0b493f296ac496f6bdf081c55956",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 3,
              "character": 3,
              "craft": 3,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 3
            },
            "overall": 3.2,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0009",
          "reply": "Ah, that's grand news! Mayhaps it's best to have me on hand when she's 'bout two months from when she'll be due. That way, I'll be ready for any surprises. Ye'll know better than anyone when the time draws nigh. Sl\u00e1n leat!  \n---\n{\"action\": \"nods reassuringly, offering a comforting smile\", \"mood\": \"supportive\", \"internal_thought\": \"She needs a gentle hand through this\", \"language_hints\": []}",
          "response_sha256": "7105b530c0759651554e413569b8670316431632e4497ad555a3f7815f49bd5d",
          "cache_key": "980afca9e517510a6cdc93fc809a29bf9cce9c7941048e853b45ad10f7b404aa",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 4,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 4.0,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0010",
          "reply": "Ah, Father Cathal has his own views, sure. But the old ways and our beliefs have been with us for generations. They've kept our people strong and connected to the land. Just like a good tea of thyme eases a cough, these traditions keep our spirits lifted. \n\n---\n{\"action\": \"leans back, considering\", \"mood\": \"thoughtful\", \"internal_thought\": \"Tradition holds wisdom\", \"language_hints\": []}",
          "response_sha256": "a7dcf5c33d10f0b9e3626da48dfd08043d103ec1db048668a694c816cf87e175",
          "cache_key": "5b19e9116e1322d199a201237af27a59ef506c1309fc6fa9393a24a85a0336fb",
